Fix commit: 35d5a7d. Plan-evidence commit: dcffc7b.
Branch: chore/deps-refresh. No push.

## F1: an advisory record with an unknown severity

The parser read the severity of every advisory record, but it dropped a
record whose severity was missing or unknown. A payload of `{"pkg":[{}]}`
printed zero counts and exited 0. A record with the severity `urgent` gave
the same result. The check reported a clean result when it could not
classify an advisory.

The fix in `tests/deps_audit/run.sh` checks the severity of every record
before the count and before the allowance. A severity outside critical,
high, moderate, and low is a malformed record, and the check exits 2.

## F2: an allow line without a reason

The allow parser took the first token of every line as the GHSA id. A bare
`GHSA-jp82-f5mq-hwhp` line therefore exempted the high advisory of the
case-high fixture.

The fix takes the id and the reason of every line. An entry needs both. A
bare id exempts nothing, and the advisory stays counted. The id still
matches exactly, never as a prefix.

## Regression cases (Green-owned)

`tests/deps_audit/test-r2.sh` holds four checks over three new fixtures:

- `case-missing-severity`: a record without a severity, wants exit 2.
- `case-unknown-severity`: a record with the severity `urgent`, wants exit 2.
- `case-bare-id`: an allow file with a bare id and a prefix id, wants exit 1.
- `case-bare-id-counts`: the high advisory of that case stays counted.

The Red test `tests/deps_audit/test.sh` and its fixtures stay untouched.

